-- Autostart necessary processes (like notifications daemons, status bars, etc.)
-- Or execute your favorite apps at launch like this:

-- exec-once = $terminal
-- exec-once = nm-applet &
-- exec-once = waybar & hyprpaper & firefox
-- swaync replaced mako (which replaced dunst). mako and dunst both lack any
-- animation support whatsoever -- no fade, slide or transition options exist
-- in either. swaync is GTK4, so its notifications animate via transition-time
-- in ~/.config/swaync/config.json.
-- Waybar starts through its systemd service below for automatic crash recovery.
-- Animations off when the battery is genuinely low, on otherwise. Started
-- here rather than as a systemd user unit so it inherits
-- HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE -- hyprctl needs it.
-- Animations stay enabled regardless of battery or AC power.
-- exec-once = ~/scripts/power-aware-animations.sh --watch
-- Keeps the YouTube webapp tab numbers contiguous: closing a tab would
-- otherwise leave a gap (1, 3) since the numbers live in each page title.
-- exec-once = waybar & hyprpaper & dunst
-- hypridle is supervised by systemd via hyprland-services-start.sh
-- Bring up the systemd user graphical-session.target so xdg-desktop-portal can start
-- (without this, OBS/screen-share has no PipeWire ScreenCast portal). Import env first.
-- Restore mpv/YouTube PiP floats to their pre-fullscreen spot instead of letting
-- Hyprland re-center them on fullscreen exit (regression since v0.54).
-- Clear automatic pinned MPV focus when entering an otherwise empty workspace.
-- Keep stream chat attached to the player when it moves.
-- Remember the workspace before monitor hotplug changes focus.
-- Start swayosd-server for showing volume and brightness controls on cick
-- Enable paired Bluetooth peripherals at desktop startup.
-- exec-once = while true; do swayosd-server; sleep 1; done

-- Detect hardware on boot for using external monitors
-- Ensure passwords from 1Password are correctly copied to clipboard for easy pasting
-- exec-once = wl-paste --primary --watch wl-copy
-- Auto-start kanshi for monitor hotplug detection
-- Kanshi is supervised by systemd via hyprland-services-start.sh
-- Persist the Hyprland log (normally only in /run, lost on reboot) so crashes can be diagnosed after the fact.
-- exec = kanshictl reload
-- exec-once = hyprpaper
-- exec-once = dunst
-- Start clipboard daemon to copy and paste easily in and out of terminal



